## The rule (system-agnostic — keep)

One library, three consumers. Never fork a component per consumer, never re-implement it in the
prototype or the app, never hand-type a token. A screen needs something the library can't do → build the
component here (code) or file a Figma DS gap to `{{DS_REPO}}` (design). Both prototype and app consume the
SAME published version of `{{COMPONENT_LIB}}`.

## Token sync (system-agnostic — keep)

Coded tokens are GENERATED from the published Figma DS (`{{DS_REPO}}`), not hand-typed:
1. Export the Figma variables/styles (the DS context's manifest is the key list).
2. Transform to the coded token module (names/keys mirror the manifest so a Figma change is a mechanical regen).
3. Commit; diff against the last sync. Re-run on every {{SYSTEM_NAME}} republish.

