## Consumer-parity rule (system-agnostic — keep)

Every export must resolve for EVERY consumer that imports it. A fork that covers one consumer and not the
other dies on an undefined import — and only when the component is finally used, not at build. When a
component must fork, note the fork and its reason here.

## Parity gate (system-agnostic — keep)

A component is done when: it matches its Figma source (verified by a Storybook screenshot vs the Figma
render), every value is token-bound (no literals), states are complete + accessible (44×44, focus,
roles/labels, reduced-motion), and it renders in every consumer.

